[Defining a struct] ! it does not create any variables
the syntax is as follows:
struct NameOfStruct
{
	datatype1 dataMember1;
	datatype2 dataMember2;
	...
};

[instances] ! it is not a variable and no memory is created at that point.
the syntax is as follows:
struct NameOfStruct variableName;

[Initializing a Struct] ! Each value will be assigned to the data members in the order that the data members are declared.
struct Student student1 ={ "Amy", "Lee", 123456789, "CPA", 3.7};

[Accessing data members] ! use the dot operator (.)
... instanceVariable.datamember ...
